course: dictionary
lesson: 2455
title: Dangle: hanging loose or tempting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word dangle means to hang down loosely and swing. Think of a monkey's tail, or dangling earrings that swing when you move your head. Dangles and dangling are other forms of the same word.
explain: Context helps here. «An anglerfish dangles a glowing lure in front of its mouth.» The lure hangs down and moves, and the fish uses it like bait to tempt small fish. So dangle can also mean holding something so it hangs loosely, or offering something to tempt someone.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "The lure hangs loosely in front of its mouth" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Dangle means to hang down loosely and swing.
fact: To dangle something means to hold it so that it hangs loosely.
fact: To dangle something in front of someone means to offer it to tempt them.
fact: «An anglerfish dangles a glowing lure» in the deep sea, to tempt fish closer.
fact: Loose cords and cables that dangle can be dangerous for small children, so keep them out of reach.
exercise: «An anglerfish dangles a glowing lure in front of its mouth.» What is the anglerfish doing with its lure? | Hiding it under a rock | Swallowing it whole | Holding it still on the seabed | *Holding it so it hangs loosely, to tempt its prey
exercise: «Her dangling earrings swung as she laughed.» What do dangling earrings do? | *Hang down loosely and swing | Fall off every day | Shine in the dark | Stay flat against the ear
exercise: «Loose cords that dangle can be dangerous for small children.» Why can dangling cords be dangerous? | *A small child could trip on them or pull them down | Cords are always hot | Small children cannot see cords at all | They make the room too dark
test: Jayden says dangle means to drop quickly and land with a bang. What does dangle really mean? | To stand very still | *To hang down loosely and swing | To drop quickly and land with a bang | To make a loud noise
test: «Tom dangled his legs over the edge of the wall.» What did Tom do? | Hid his legs under a blanket | *Let his legs hang down loosely | Pulled his legs up tight | Ran along the top of the wall
exam: Which sentence uses dangle to mean offering something to tempt someone? | The cat dangled from the tall tree. | The rope was old and dangled in the garden. | *Mia dangled a shiny coin in front of the cat to tempt it closer. | The bell dangled in the wind.
